The photo-real splat tier (backend/repairos/recreation/splat.py, run on the GPU pod only) uses gsplat
(https://github.com/nerfstudio-project/gsplat, v1.5.3), Copyright the gsplat authors, Apache License 2.0. It is not
vendored: deploy/runpod/bootstrap.sh installs it on the pod (LEA_SPLAT=1) from deploy/runpod/requirements.splat.lock
(hash-pinned) and compiles its CUDA kernels there. gsplat bundles OpenGL Mathematics (GLM), MIT License (or the
Happy Bunny License). The original Inria 3D Gaussian Splatting code (non-commercial) is not used.
